  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e81bb16ba40385c4bb6dac73ed24daa7, type: 3}
  m_Name: ModelCard
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SimuLean.Unity.SimuLeanModelCard
  displayName: "M/M/1 queue \u2014 validated against queueing theory"
  description: 'The textbook single-server queue, set up so its results can be checked against queueing theory: the first flow of SimuLean and its validation (docs/guide/validation.md).'
  author: SimuLean
  scenePath: Assets/Scenes/Validation/MM1.unity
  copiedFrom: 
  created: 2026-11-09 12:00:00
  modified: 2026-11-09 12:00:00
  represents: 'An M/M/1 queue: Arrivals (Source, Poisson: exponential gaps, rate lambda = 0.8 per min) -> Queue (unlimited) -> Server (Multi-Server, capacity 1, exponential service, rate mu = 1 per min) -> Exit, which tallies time_in_system = age.'
  kpis: 'Wq=Queue.stay_avg, Lq=Queue.content_avg, W=Exit.tally:time_in_system:mean, rho=Server.utilization, derived L=Lq+rho.

    Theory (rho = lambda/mu = 0.8): Wq = rho/(mu - lambda) = 4 min, Lq = rho^2/(1 - rho) = 3.2, W = 1/(mu - lambda) = 5 min, L = rho/(1 - rho) = 4, utilisation 0.8.

    Simulated, seeds 1..10, 18000 observed min each (2026-10-21): Wq 3.96 +- 0.17, Lq 3.18 +- 0.15, W 4.95 +- 0.17, L 3.98 +- 0.15, rho 0.801 +- 0.006 (95 % half-widths): every theoretical value is inside its interval. MM1ValidationTests checks 5 replications within a few percent.'
  parameters: 'Arrival rate Arrivals.interArrivalDistribution.exponentialRate (0.8 per min) and service rate Server.delayStrategy.exponentialRate (1 per min): keep lambda < mu, and compare with the formulas for the new rho. Server.capacity > 1 turns it into an M/M/c (compare with Erlang C).'
  assumptions: 'Time unit min, horizon 20000 min with a warm-up of 2000 min (statistics over the last 18000 min, so the empty start does not bias them), fixed seed 1. Unlimited queue, FIFO, one server, no downtime. Steady-state theory: short runs or few replications scatter around it.'
